Synthetic signing fixtures (decision 0009). Nothing in this directory belongs to an account.

- The secp256k1 signing key in the header of hibachi-vectors.tsv is SHA-256 of the made-up
  phrase on its key_phrase line, "fueledbychai-rs FBC-8mzv synthetic Hibachi signing key,
  belonging to no account", chosen for these vectors alone (HibachiSignOracle.java computes it
  from the phrase, and the Rust tests check that it does). It is no key of the owner's or of any
  Hibachi account, it was never derived from any account's seed, and it is neither the EIP-155
  example key the Java library's EcdsaHibachiSignerTest uses nor the web3 documentation key in
  fixtures/paradex/signing/signbench. The public_key line is that key's public key.
- The orders, cancels and nonces are made-up inputs. Contract id 1 with decimals 9 and 6 and
  ETH/USDT-P's tick and step are the public example values of api-doc.hibachi.xyz and the SDK's
  test data; the docs_* rows are the worked examples printed on Hibachi's public signing pages
  (README.md cites them); the java_test_* rows are the inputs of the public Java library's
  HibachiPayloadPackerTest; the random_* rows are drawn from java.util.Random with the seed in
  the header. Apart from the docs' printed examples, no order id, nonce or contract here was
  seen on Hibachi.
- Every other long hex value (payloads, SHA-256 digests, signatures) is computed from those
  inputs by the Java library's packer and signer. hibachi-vectors.tsv repeats the key in its
  header so the Rust tests read it from here and no key-shaped value sits in crates/.

This marker covers fixtures/hibachi/signing/ only. Recorded Hibachi frames or answers never go
here; fixtures/hibachi/rest/ has its own marker.
